<title>UK: Pillar sells Glasgow building to BT.</title>
<headline>Pillar sells Glasgow building to BT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property company Pillar Property Investments Plc said on Monday that it has exchanged contracts with British Telecommunications Plc for the development of a new office building in Glasgow, Scotland.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the sale of the 180,000 square feet building to BT represents some 31 percent of the total Broomielaw, Glasgow development.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a ringing endorsement for Glasgow and for our site and we look forward to a thoroughly successful development on BT's behalf,&quot; said Patrick Vaughan, chief executive of Pillar.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
